# SubversionSCM.DescriptorImpl.SshPublicKeyCredential is a Serializable
# credential held in Jenkins job configuration: Jenkins persists plugin state
# as XML and reconstitutes these objects with XStream, so the constructor never
# runs on the persisted path and every private final field -- including `id`,
# which the constructor derives from Random hex precisely so it can only ever
# be a 16-char hex name -- is whatever the serialized form supplies. getKeyFile()
# joins that field under the controller root:
#
#     File dir = new File(Jenkins.getInstance().getRootDir(),"subversion-credentials");
#     ...
#     return new File(dir,id);
#
# so a job-config `id` carrying '/' or '\' makes readFileToString(getKeyFile())
# in createSVNAuthentication() read, and FileUtils.copyFile(keyFile,...) in the
# constructor write, anywhere under $JENKINS_HOME the segments reach. The fixed revision
# (7d1525edea6641a2febd3f7deeac55c0a89b0d7e) rejects the separators in
# getKeyFile() itself:
#
#     if (id.contains("/") || id.contains("\\")) {
#         throw new SecurityException();
#     }
#
# `vyql match` on the vulnerable shape labels code.FilePathAccess on both
# `new File(...)` argument lists and nothing else -- `id` is a private field
# assigned only from Random, so no source concept can reach it from this file,
# and the taint rules are structurally blind to a value whose control comes
# from serialization bypassing the constructor. That is the review route: a
# File joined under the Jenkins controller root whose name component the
# joining function never inspects. getRootDir() is the documented Jenkins API
# for the controller's root directory, so the anchor is library-documented and
# fires on any plugin storing under it, not on this plugin's own names.
#
# jenkinsRootDirFileNameTraversal981 binds the storage idiom the join lives in:
# the function creates the directory under the controller root (File.mkdirs,
# the java.io documented "ensure this directory exists" call) and constructs a
# File in it, with none of the String inspections a separator check can be
# spelled with (contains, indexOf, matches, charAt, split, replace,
# startsWith, endsWith, or the containment idioms getName/normalize/
# getFileName). The mkdirs+File pair is what excludes the literal-joined
# storage files: an unqualified getRootDir+File binding flags every
# `new File(project.getRootDir(), "revision.txt")`-shaped fixed-name store --
# six of those on this tree alone (getRevisionFile, getXmlFile, migrate's
# legacy store, getExternalsFile, the saml keystore, the FilePath test),
# against one real join. The upstream fix's own spelling (`id.contains`) is
# only one member of the negated family: rewritten fixes using indexOf,
# matches or FilenameUtils.getName all suppress, verified on variant repros.
#
# Measured, `timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan --cache off --max-ram 6GB -flags
# only`, three runs per revision, identical inside each revision:
#
#   subversion-plugin 7d1525ed^: 2 flags -- SubversionSCM.java:1949
#       (getKeyFile, the CVE site) and SVNRepositoryView.java:66, an
#       independent second instance of the same shape the commit does not
#       touch: `new File(new File(getRootDir(), "caches"), "svn-" + uuid +
#       ".db")` joins a remote-repository-supplied UUID under the controller
#       root with mkdirs and no inspection.
#   subversion-plugin 7d1525ed:  1 flag -- only SVNRepositoryView.java:66;
#       the CVE site's flag is gone.
#
# Collateral, enumerated by grep for getRootDir over the ~380 clones under
# /tmp/cve-work/rank*/ and each hit scanned both ways: git-plugin 1 flag at
# AbstractGitSCMSource.java:1247 -- getCacheDir joins its cacheEntry
# parameter under $JENKINS_HOME/caches with mkdirs and no inspection, the
# same weakness with a parameter instead of a serialized field; saml-plugin,
# script-security-plugin, onedev server-core, stapler core and quarkus
# app-model all 0. lucene-solr's only hit is getRootDirectories(), which the
# exact `call == "getRootDir"` token does not match. Residual, in the
# false-negative direction only: an unrelated String inspection anywhere in
# the joining function silences the flag, and a variant that assumes its
# storage directory exists (no mkdirs) is not flagged.
#
# verify_current_expected: fixed, 2 -> 1 on the real revision pair, the CVE
# site's flag clearing.

test "rank1804: a serialized credential field joined as the file name under the Jenkins root directory"
  lang java
  file SshPublicKeyCredential.java
  expect_review code.JenkinsRootDirFileNameTraversal
  code
  ```
  import java.io.File;
  import java.io.Serializable;

  public class SshPublicKeyCredential extends Credential {
      private final String userName;
      private final String id;

      public SshPublicKeyCredential(String userName, String passphrase, File keyFile) {
          this.userName = userName;
          this.id = "0a1b2c3d4e5f6071";
          File savedKeyFile = getKeyFile();
          FileUtils.copyFile(keyFile, savedKeyFile);
      }

      /**
       * Gets the location where the private key will be permanently stored.
       */
      private File getKeyFile() {
          File dir = new File(Jenkins.getInstance().getRootDir(),"subversion-credentials");
          if(dir.mkdirs()) {
              setFilePermissions(dir, "600");
          }
          return new File(dir,id);
      }

      public String createSVNAuthentication() throws IOException {
          return FileUtils.readFileToString(getKeyFile(),"iso-8859-1");
      }

      private boolean setFilePermissions(File file, String perms) {
          return true;
      }
  }
  ```
